^(?<prefix_i><line-height=90%>)?(?<first>(?:They\ found\ the\ lute\.\ I\ suppose\ I\ didn't\ realize\ how\ far\ Bernardo\ and\ Hamlet\ had\ drifted\ apart\ over\ the\ years,\ and\ how\ bad\ things\ had\ gotten\ between\ Hamlet\ and\ my\ brother\.\ All\ this\ time,\ it\ seemed\ natural\ to\ assume\ we\ were\ no\ less\ close\ than\ we'd\ always\ been,\ but\ time\ changes\ things\.\ I\ wonder\ if\ it's\ too\ late\ for\ Hamlet\ and\ my\ brother\ to\ make\ amends\.\ If\ Laertes\ and\ Hamlet\ could\ only\ meet,\ I\ know\ something\ good\ might\ finally\ come\ of\ it\.|Hamlet\ returned\ the\ found\ lute\ to\ Laertes\.\ At\ first,\ Laertes\ was\ furious,\ but\ I\ think\ the\ conversation\ was\ many\ years\ in\ its\ formation\.\ It\ seemed\ to\ be\ cathartic,\ in\ a\ way;\ they\ understand\ one\ another\ better\ now,\ at\ least\.\ Perhaps\ I\ can\ leverage\ this\ to\ help\ them\ keep\ the\ peace\ in\ the\ future\.|I\ found\ a\ note\ from\ my\ brother\ discussing\ a\ lute\ he\ believes\ was\ stolen\.\ He\ thinks\ Hamlet\ made\ off\ with\ it\.\ Laertes\ and\ Hamlet\ have\ always\ had\ a\ contentious\ relationship,\ to\ say\ the\ least\.\ I\ wonder\ if\ I\ can\ help\ resolve\ this\ situation\.|As\ soon\ as\ Hamlet\ and\ Bernardo\ had\ a\ chance\ to\ meet,\ they\ quickly\ realized\ that\ the\ lute\ was\ lost,\ not\ stolen\.\ They\ expect\ to\ spend\ some\ time\ over\ the\ next\ few\ days\ on\ a\ wild\ chase\ 'round\ the\ castle\ to\ find\ it\.))(?<separator_i>

