^(?<prefix_i><line-height=90%>)?(?<first>(?:Rosencrantz,\ obviously\ heartbroken,\ planned\ Guilda's\ funeral\ as\ expected\.\ At\ the\ very\ end,\ Guilda\ popped\ out\ and\ was\.\.\.\ unpleasantly\ surprised\ at\ the\ lack\ of\ attendance\.\ She's\ now\ decided\ that\ 'nothing\ matters'\ and\ 'we're\ all\ unimportant\ in\ the\ scheme\ of\ the\ universe'\ and\ other\ related\ nonsense\.\ She's\ decided\ to\ plan\ a\ party\ for\ all\ of\ the\ other\ 'unimportant'\ folks\ in\ the\ castle\ and\ I'm\ invited\.\ Insulting,\ yes,\ but\ I\ <i>do</i>\ like\ a\ good\ party\.|I\ attended\ Guilda's\ little\ party,\ and\ at\ the\ end\ of\ it,\ I\ realized\ something\ horrible:\ She's\ going\ to\ die\ in\ earnest\ aboard\ that\ ship\.\ They\ both\ are\.\ And\ <i>I</i>\ have\ the\ power\ to\ save\ them\.\ I\ can\ get\ on\ board\ and\ ensure\ Guilda\ lives\.\ But\ first,\ I\ need\ to\ make\ sure\ I'm\ present\ when\ Hamlet\ and\ company\ sail\ for\ England\ on\ Saturday\ morning\.|Guilda\ invited\ me\ to\ leave\ the\ castle\ with\ her\ and\ Rosencrantz\ forever\.\ They\ want\ to\ gallivant\ around\ the\ countryside,\ selfishly\ forgetting\ and\ foregoing\ everything\ but\ their\ own\ worldly\ pleasure\.\ Could\ I\ be\ happy,\ living\ such\ a\ life\?|Somehow\ Lady\ Guildenstern's\ gotten\ the\ idea\ that\ she\ could\ pretend\ to\ be\ dead,\ and\ she\ finds\ it\ rather\ funny\.\ So\ funny,\ in\ fact,\ that\ she's\ asked\ me\ to\ tell\ everyone\ she\ really\ <i>is</i>\ dead\.\ This\ can't\ end\ well\.|I\ met\ Guilda\ on\ the\ deck,\ and\ she\ called\ me\ her\ 'good\ friend'\ for\ the\ first\ time\.\ She\ might\ be\ the\ first\ true\ friend\ I've\ made\ in\ Elsinore\ recently\.|Guilda\ invited\ me\ to\ meet\ her\ on\ the\ foredeck\.\ I\ wonder\ what\ she\ wants\ to\ discuss\?\ Meanwhile,\ I\ need\ to\ find\ a\ way\ to\ avert\ this\ impending\ crisis\.|I\ met\ Guilda\ on\ the\ deck,\ and\ there\ was\ a\.\.\.\ moment,\ of\ sorts\.\ I\ wonder,\ if\ we\ had\ more\ time\ together\.\.\.))(?