^(?<prefix_i><line-height=90%>)?(?<first>(?:I've\ obtained\ proof\ that\ Gertrude\ and\ Claudius's\ affair\ started\ before\ King\ Hamlet's\ death\.\ When\ I\ told\ Hamlet,\ he\ was\ fully\ consumed\ by\ his\ desire\ for\ revenge\.\ He\ seems\ to\ have\ a\ plan\ he\ intends\ to\ execute\ during\ the\ time\ period\ when\ we\ would\ all\ ordinarily\ have\ gathered\ to\ watch\ Peter\ Quince's\ performance\.\ I\ have\ a\ bad\ feeling\ about\ this,\ but\ if\ I\ want\ to\ meet\ this\ so\-called\ ghost,\ I'll\ need\ to\ see\ this\ through\ to\ its\ end\.|I've\ obtained\ proof\ that\ Gertrude\ and\ Claudius's\ affair\ started\ before\ King\ Hamlet's\ death\.\ If\ I\ let\ Hamlet\ know\ what\ I\ found,\ I'm\ certain\ he'll\ do\ something\ rash\.\ But\ if\ that's\ what\ it\ takes\ to\ understand\ what's\ happening,\ perhaps\ it's\ wiser\ for\ me\ to\ follow\ this\ to\ its\ conclusion,\ no\ matter\ what\.|Hamlet\ and\ others\ have\ seen\ a\ spirit\ of\ King\ Hamlet\ haunting\ the\ castle\.\ This\ is\ how\ he\ learned\ of\ Claudius's\ deeds\.\ If\ the\ ghost\ is\ indeed\ real,\ maybe\ there\ is\ a\ way\ for\ me\ to\ meet\ it\.\ Surely\ Hamlet\ knows\ something\.|Hamlet\ is\ tight\-lipped\ on\ the\ spirit—he\ needs\ to\ be\ sure\ he\ can\ trust\ me\.\ He's\ asked\ me\ to\ get\ information\ from\ a\ diary\ his\ mother\ keeps\ in\ her\ room\.\ Well,\ if\ it's\ what\ must\ be\ done,\ then\ so\ be\ it\.|Some\ truly\ horrific\ acts\ occurred,\ but\ in\ the\ end,\ the\ spirit\ appeared\.\ King\ Hamlet\ spoke\ to\ me\.\ He\ waits\ on\ the\ walls\ each\ night\ at\ midnight\.\ I've\ been\ asked\ to\ seek\ him\ out\.))(?<separator_i>

