^(?<prefix_i><line-height=90%>)?(?<first>(?:Irma's\ desire\ to\ discipline\ Hamlet\ ultimately\ degraded\ into\ a\ poisoning\ attempt\ which\ took\ the\ lives\ of\ the\ King,\ Queen,\ and\ herself\.\ The\ people\ I\ love\ are\ capable\ of\ such\ horrors\.\ It's\ frightening\ to\ think\ about\.\ But\ I\ feel\ as\ though\ I\ understand\ a\ little\ better\ some\ of\ the\ tension\ bubbling\ just\ beneath\ the\ surface\.\ And\ there's\ a\ possibility\.\.\.\ that\ what\ happened\ here\ might\ help\ me,\ somehow,\ in\ the\ future\.|I\ can\ hardly\ believe\ what\ came\ of\ all\ this\.\ Irma\ poisoned\ Gertrude\ and\ Claudius\ to\ death\.\ Not\ intentionally,\ of\ course;\ she\ was\ trying\ to\ eliminate\ Hamlet\.\ But\ she\ was\ summarily\ thrown\ in\ the\ dungeon\.\ I\ don't\ want\ to\ think\ about\ what\ Hamlet\ might\ do\ to\ her\ next,\ but\ I\ feel\ some\ obligation\ to\ see\ this\ horrible\ world\ run\ its\ course\.|Irma\ believes\ Hamlet\ is\ in\ need\ of\ some\ long\-overdue\ discipline,\ and\ I've\ heard\ her\ grumbling\ to\ the\ Queen\ about\ it\.\ There's\ no\ doubt\ that\ Hamlet's\ been\ difficult\ for\ everyone\ in\ Elsinore\ to\ handle\.\ I\ wonder\ if\ I\ can\ force\ the\ issue\ to\ a\ resolution\.|I\ saw\ Hamlet\ and\ Irma\ meet,\ and\ the\ both\ of\ them\ fared\ worse\ for\ it\.\ Hamlet\ was\ cruel\ and\ Irma\ only\ fed\ the\ flames\.\ I\ sense\ something\ must\ come\ to\ a\ head\ sometime\ soon\.))(?<separator_i>

