^(?<prefix_i><line-height=90%>)?(?<first>(?:I've\ learned\ that\ my\ mother\ Elise\ kept\ an\ account\ of\ Astrid's\ story\.\.\.\ and\ it\ might\ exist\ somewhere\.\ My\ mother\ contracted\ plague\ and\ was\ sent\ away\ to\ die\ in\ a\ sanitarium\ off\ the\ southern\ coast,\ alone\ and\ frightened,\ by\ King\ Hamlet\.\ After\ she\ perished,\ her\ belongings—along\ with\ those\ of\ other\ victims—were\ brought\ back\ by\ ship\ and\ sealed\ in\ a\ small\ shed\ near\ the\ docks\.\ Perhaps\ I\ can\ learn\ more\ information\ there,\ if\ I\ can\ find\ a\ way\ in\.|The\ tale\ of\ Queen\ Astrid\ turned\ out\ to\ be\ a\ complex\ one,\ involving\ her\ husband,\ his\ mistress,\ Simona,\ and\.\.\.\ my\ mother\.\ I\ got\ help\ retrieving\ my\ mother's\ belongings\ from\ the\ shack\ on\ the\ docks,\ and\ the\ notes\ she\ kept\ were\.\.\.\ strange,\ to\ say\ the\ least\.\ Simona\ was\ trapped\ in\ a\ loop\ as\ well,\ it\ seems,\ but\ what\ was\ this\ about\ a\ book\?\ About\ choosing\ to\ be\ Queen\?\ And\ could\ she\ really\ have\ escaped\ Elsinore\ alive\?|If\ I\ talk\ to\ Father\ about\ Queen\ Astrid,\ he\ acts\ evasive\.\ Evidently,\ the\ Queen\ was\ quite\ close\ to\ my\ mother,\ and\ he\ finds\ it\ painful\ to\ discuss\ her\.\ He\ mentioned\ that\ he\ visits\ her\ grave\ Thursday\ night,\ though\.\.\.|King\ Hamlet\ expressed\ to\ me\ that\ his\ mother,\ Queen\ Astrid,\ may\ have\ also\ experienced\ loops\.\ I've\ grown\ up\ hearing\ so\ little\ about\ her\ and\ her\ legacy\.\ There\ must\ be\ more\ to\ find\.|In\ various\ places,\ I've\ heard\ mention\ of\ Queen\ Astrid—Hamlet's\ grandmother—but\ I've\ realized\ I\ don't\ know\ much\ about\ her\ reign\.\ I\ could\ ask\ around\ to\ learn\ more\.))(?<separator_i>

