^(?<prefix_i><line-height=90%>)?(?<first>(?:Hamlet's\ actions\ and\ plans\ seem\ to\ have\ borne\ fruit—after\ the\ play,\ King\ Claudius\ confessed\ to\ God\ that\ he\ was\ the\ snake\ who\ killed\ Hamlet's\ father\.\ The\ revelation\ was\ stunning,\ but\ Hamlet\ was\ strangely\ unsurprised\.\.\.\ his\ actions\ indicate\ he\ already\ knew\?\ Where\ could\ he\ have\ gotten\ his\ information\?|Hamlet's\ madness\ was\ brought\ on\ not\ by\ love,\ but\ by\ a\ meeting\ with\ what\ he\ believes\ to\ be\ the\ spirit\ of\ his\ father\.\ It's\ from\ there\ he\ must\ have\ gotten\ his\ information\ about\ Claudius's\ murder\.\ But\ the\ information\ turned\ out\ to\ be\ correct—so\ does\ this\ spirit\ actually\ exist\?|In\ the\ gallery,\ I\ found\ a\ clue\ as\ to\ Hamlet's\ madness\.\ Apparently,\ he's\ been\ obsessing\ over\ some\ irregularities\ in\ his\ father's\ death\ report\.\ Clearly,\ Hamlet\ suspects\ there\ is\ more\ to\ this\ story—but\ what\ is\ he\ hoping\ to\ accomplish\?|Hamlet\ showed\ up\ in\ my\ room,\ raving\ incomprehensibly\.\ He's\ been\ difficult\ before,\ but\ this\ is\ strange\ even\ for\ him\.\ What\ could\ be\ causing\ him\ to\ act\ out\ like\ this\?|I've\ been\ pointed\ towards\ the\ gallery—perhaps\ something\ exists\ there\ that\ could\ give\ me\ some\ clue\ as\ to\ the\ origin\ of\ Hamlet's\ recent\ bout\ of\ madness\.|It\ seems\ that\ Hamlet\ is\ concentrating\ most\ of\ his\ energy\ on\ putting\ on\ a\ play\ for\ this\ Saturday\.\ Something's\ brewing\.\ I\ feel\ uneasy\ about\ this\.))(?<separator_i>

